@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Mobile SMS verification and account access (phase 7)
+
+Implemented locally on November 10, 2026. The team has no SMS provider account yet. The Semaphore adapter is implemented and tested with a mocked gateway; no real text, paid service, account signup or production deployment was performed. The local private environment remains DEVELOPMENT, with its existing secret and saved accounts.
+
+## Apply
+
+On backend `42b4552`, apply `mobile-v4.patch`, `mobile-claims.patch`, `mobile-notifications.patch`, then `mobile-sms.patch`. Generate Prisma and deploy migrations to a separate test/development database before starting the API. This phase adds OTP delivery mode/acceptance time and session authentication mode; earlier credentials are tagged DEVELOPMENT and existing development challenges retain their acceptance time. No dependency or Redis worker is added.
+
+## Activate SMS when the team is ready
+
+1. Set up the team's Semaphore account, API key, credit balance and registered default or approved sender name. Review the current [official API documentation](https://www.semaphore.co/docs) and provider account terms before buying credits. Sender approval and carrier delivery are external requirements.
+2. Keep the API key in the backend's private environment or hosted secret manager. Never put it in mobile code, an EXPO_PUBLIC variable, screenshots, Git or chat. Keep MOBILE_AUTH_SECRET private and stable; it also protects mobile session/QR operations.
+3. In a separate configured backend instance, set:
+
+   ```dotenv
+   MOBILE_AUTH_MODE=SMS
+   MOBILE_AUTH_SECRET=<existing-private-mobile-secret>
+   MOBILE_SMS_SEMAPHORE_API_KEY=<private-api-key>
+   # Optional: an approved sender, otherwise use the account's registered default.
+   MOBILE_SMS_SENDER_NAME=<approved-sender-name>
+   MOBILE_SMS_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
+   ```
+
+   Replace the placeholders privately. Omit the sender variable if using the registered default. The local demo can remain MOBILE_AUTH_MODE=DEVELOPMENT until the account is ready; DISABLED remains the template default. Production configuration must also satisfy the shared backend's normal HTTPS, secrets, CORS, storage and deployment requirements.
+4. Restart that API instance. Point mobile at it with the existing public API URL setting. Register a unique fictional test beneficiary using a real Philippine number you control. SMS mode returns expiry information, never a development code. A prior staff record still requires authorized linking; this feature does not link records automatically.
+5. Enter the received code. Test login, resend after 60 seconds, incorrect/expired codes, and recovery. Confirm a local phone number's receipt through the provider dashboard and the phone itself before claiming live delivery works.
+
+The adapter uses one fixed HTTPS Semaphore message endpoint and one normalized Philippine recipient. It preserves the generated six digits, including leading zeros, in a short message. No automatic provider retry or bulk send occurs. A gateway acceptance is not a carrier delivery guarantee. Provider requests are billable when activated; the prototype does not purchase credits or activate an account.
+
+## Authentication behavior
+
+Registration/challenge creation commits before the network request, so the gateway never holds a database lock. A pending SMS challenge cannot authenticate until its request is accepted. Timeout, malformed/failed gateway responses and acceptance-save failure invalidate the challenge and return a sanitized error. No raw gateway response, API key or OTP is logged, audited or returned in SMS mode. Only the HMAC of the code is stored. A failed initial send leaves one unverified account that can resume registration after the resend cooldown.
+
+Codes expire after five minutes, allow five incorrect attempts, have a one-minute resend cooldown and remain single-use under the existing account lock. Mode binding prevents DEVELOPMENT codes or sessions being used in SMS mode and vice versa. Switching modes requires signing in again. No secret or private .env is changed by this patch. Existing demo QR records, claims, wallet history, staff passwords and authenticators are not modified.
+
+## Recovery
+
+The mobile Recover account screen now requests a real login challenge and opens the existing OTP verification screen after the server confirms the request. Development codes are displayed only when explicitly returned by the development backend. It does not create a password, reset an identity, approve enrollment or create a session before code verification. People who no longer control the registered number are directed to the facilitator; a lost-number linking/reassignment workflow is separate work. Existing other sessions still follow their ordinary logout/expiry rules.
+
+Recovery disables repeated sends/phone edits while waiting, preserves failed input, supports retry, ignores responses after leaving, and uses EN/BS copy. The public recovery page omits signed-in navigation. Registration and code-request client timeouts allow 20 seconds for the configured gateway deadline plus database work. The original mobile backend remains compatible.
+
+## Checks
+
+- Mobile regressions, TypeScript and web/Android exports.
+- `node --test test/mobile-sms.test.js`: only mocked requests, including leading zero, sender handling, failed/malformed replies, timeout, no retry and sanitized errors.
+- With explicit DATABASE_URL for a separate migrated test instance and RUN_MOBILE_DB_TESTS=1: `node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/mobile-auth.integration.js test/mobile-sms.integration.js`. The SMS test intercepts all gateway requests and exercises pending delivery, successful issuance, hidden codes, registration retry, failed-send invalidation, cooldown, recovery/login, single use and mode separation.
+- From mobile, `npm.cmd run test:shared` covers the preceding shared account/document/schedule/QR/release/notification flows in DEVELOPMENT. Keep database suites sequential.
+
+Actual provider credentials, account credits/sender approval, receipt on a physical phone and hosted deployment remain required for live SMS validation.
